Originally submitted by benlitchfield on 2004-12-04 11:43.<br/>
<br/>
Certain fields have the font automatically resized as the <br/>
user types text such that all of the text will fit in the <br/>
box, shrinking the text when there is too much text.  <br/>
<br/>
PDFBox does not do this attached is an example PDF <br/>
document.<br/>
<br/>
BJL:Looked into this a little bit but it I don&#39;t see how to <br/>
determine that the font size should be automatically <br/>
resized versus scrolled.  Need to look into flags in more <br/>
detail.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
[attachment on SourceForge]<br/>
http://sourceforge.net/tracker/download.php?group_id=78314&amp;atid=552832&amp;aid=1079010&amp;file_id=111281<br/>
before-original.pdf (), 82709 bytes<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
[comment on SourceForge]<br/>
Originally sent by benlitchfield.<br/>
Logged In: YES <br/>
user_id=601708<br/>
<br/>
Finally, I found where this is set.  In PDF Reference 1.6 pg <br/>
641 last sentence in second to last paragraph.  Now I just <br/>
need to fix it.<br/>
<br/>
&quot;A zero value for size means that the font is to be autosized:<br/>
its size is computed as a function of the height of the <br/>
annotation rectangle.&quot;
