http://sourceforge.net/tracker/index.php?group_id=78314&amp;atid=552832&amp;aid=1181857<br/>
Originally submitted by ng_aldridge on 2005-04-12 15:30.<br/>
<br/>
I am getting a NullPointerException from<br/>
PDRadioCollection.getValue (). It seems that my radio<br/>
collection dictionaries don&#39;t have kids so the<br/>
kids.size () call fails:<br/>
<br/>
Line 131:<br/>
<br/>
        for (int i = 0; i &lt; kids.size(); i++)<br/>
        {<br/>
            PDCheckbox btn = (PDCheckbox)kids.get(i);<br/>
            if( btn.isChecked() )<br/>
            {<br/>
                retval = btn.getOnValue();<br/>
            }<br/>
        }<br/>
        if( retval == null )<br/>
        {<br/>
            retval = getDictionary().getNameAsString(<br/>
&quot;V&quot; );<br/>
        }<br/>
<br/>
I added a check for null value of kids and things<br/>
behaved properly. If you need a sample PDF that shows<br/>
this behaviour, I&#39;ll upload one.<br/>
<br/>
Cheers,<br/>
<br/>
Nathan<br/>
<br/>
