http://sourceforge.net/tracker/index.php?group_id=78314&amp;atid=552832&amp;aid=1305398<br/>
Originally submitted by benlitchfield on 2005-09-26 18:49.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ve run a simple test.<br/>
<br/>
Initially loading an already encrypted document, then <br/>
decrypting etc.<br/>
<br/>
PDDocument x = PDDocument.load<br/>
(&quot;/home/paul/pdfsin/encrypted.pdf&quot;);<br/>
x.decrypt(&quot;pass&quot;);<br/>
   <br/>
x.save(&quot;/home/paul/pdfsout/decrypt1.pdf&quot;);<br/>
   <br/>
x.setEncryptionDictionary(new PDStandardEncryption());<br/>
x.encrypt(&quot;pass&quot;,null);<br/>
   <br/>
x.save(&quot;/home/paul/pdfsout/encrypt1.pdf&quot;);<br/>
   <br/>
x.decrypt(&quot;pass&quot;);<br/>
x.save(&quot;/home/paul/pdfsout/decrypt2.pdf&quot;);<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
The net result of this is that the decryption on the pre-<br/>
encrypted works ok,<br/>
the subsequent re-encryption works fine. (checked <br/>
documents in acrobat, document<br/>
info OK, pages look OK and security settings as <br/>
expected)<br/>
<br/>
The final decyption however fails and the <br/>
resultant &quot;decrypt2.pdf&quot; is all white<br/>
pages. If I modify the above to reload the &quot;encrypt1.pdf&quot; <br/>
file, do the decrypt<br/>
and save then the final output is fine, so it is just the in <br/>
memory version<br/>
of the PDF after encryption is non-decryptable, which of <br/>
course can fairly easily<br/>
be worked around.
