http://sourceforge.net/tracker/index.php?group_id=78314&amp;atid=552832&amp;aid=1482334<br/>
Originally submitted by mmajis on 2006-05-05 02:30.<br/>
<br/>
If I take an XFA PDF, remove the XFA form, rename one<br/>
of the AcroForm fields and open the resulting PDF in<br/>
Acrobat, the field name is garbled.<br/>
<br/>
To begin with, it seems the field name is UTF-16BE<br/>
encoded. PDFBox writes the new /T entry in ISO-8859-1<br/>
since it finds no character values larger than 255. if<br/>
I change the source code to write UTF-16BE with the two<br/>
prefix bytes 0xFF and 0xFE (not sure of the byte order<br/>
here), the field name shows correctly in Acrobat.
