<br/>
When assigning a value to PDField &quot;AI_PLZ_ORT&quot;<br/>
containing a german &quot;Umlaut&quot; (e.g. a/o/u-dieresis -&gt;<br/>
Ã¤Ã¶Ã¼) acrobat reader is displaying a cedilla instead of<br/>
a udieresis. But if you select the Field (click into)<br/>
the the value is show in the right encoding.<br/>
A \374 in PDFDocEncoding (udieresis) is inserted and a<br/>
\374 in MacRomanEncoding (cedilla) is shown.<br/>
The PDF (orig.pdf) has been created on a Mac and the<br/>
Java application to modify the PDF runs under Windows<br/>
XP (PDFUtil.java, PDFUtil.class)<br/>
<br/>
--<br/>
javac -cp lib/PDFBox-0.7.2.jar -source 1.3 -target 1.3<br/>
PDFUtil.java<br/>
java -cp lib/PDFBox-0.7.2.jar;. PDFUtil<br/>
