http://sourceforge.net/tracker/index.php?group_id=78314&amp;atid=552832&amp;aid=1608840<br/>
Originally submitted by jlynch16 on 2006-12-04 15:24.<br/>
<br/>
In this test, I have &quot;shrunken&quot; 4 pdf pages into 1 pdf page. What this gives us is 4 XObject&#39;s that hold all the data for each original page. When shrunken, the text gets printed correctly, but the &quot;rectangle&quot; highlights on the page do not.  It&#39;s as if the graphics object doesn&#39;t know of the transformation at run time.<br/>
<br/>
In adobe, it looks fine, but in pdfBOX it gets rendered incorrectly.<br/>
<br/>
-Jim Lynch<br/>
1360 Studios<br/>
<br/>
[attachment on SourceForge]<br/>
http://sourceforge.net/tracker/download.php?group_id=78314&amp;atid=552832&amp;aid=1608840&amp;file_id=205766<br/>
4PP-Highlighting.pdf (application/pdf), 2497 bytes<br/>
4 Pages shrunken down into 1 pdf Page, with highlights.
