[comment on SourceForge]<br/>
Originally sent by tweakerbee.<br/>
Logged In: YES <br/>
user_id=1625706<br/>
Originator: NO<br/>
<br/>
This should probably be 91.-59.<br/>
<br/>
Forgot to take out the dash here. Should read: &quot;This should probably be 91.59&quot;<br/>
<br/>
[comment on SourceForge]<br/>
Originally sent by tweakerbee.<br/>
Logged In: YES <br/>
user_id=1625706<br/>
Originator: NO<br/>
<br/>
Your PDF is flawed. On the first page there is an instruction<br/>
91.-59 Tz<br/>
that is incorrect. Tz will set the textscaling (default = 100), but has to do so with a double. This should probably be 91.-59. It appears to be just before the text &quot;Emma&quot;, so maybe you can fix it with Adobe Acrobat or another editor.<br/>
<br/>
I doubt you&#39;ll get useful results though, the PDF is mostly image with OCR&#39;ed text behind it. It will contain many errors.<br/>
<br/>
HTH,<br/>
Matthijs<br/>
<br/>
