When using PDPageContentStream.drawString() characters such as é,ë,ï don&#39;t get printed or get replaced by another character. <br/>
<br/>
I assume another encoding must be used?<br/>
Where can the encoding be changed?<br/>
<br/>
The following code would sound logic to change the encoding but it doesn&#39;t seem to work;<br/>
<br/>
..<br/>
PDFont font = PDType1Font.TIMES_ROMAN <br/>
font.setEncoding(New encoding.MacRomanEncoding) <br/>
newStream.setFont(font, 8)<br/>
..<br/>
newStream.drawString(&quot;é&quot;)<br/>
..<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
An example would be greatly appreciated.
