                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      [imported from SourceForge]<br/>
http://sourceforge.net/tracker/index.php?group_id=78314&amp;atid=552834&amp;aid=1796298<br/>
Originally submitted by lintlint on 2007-09-17 08:51.<br/>
<br/>
In some files, white spaces are not defined as a character but as a distance between words. This distance is known with TextPosition.getWidthOfSpace() or TextPosition.getWidth(). In my case, WidthOfSpace was 0 and Width was Float.NaN, so extracted text contained no spaces. I just added a check on the value of this distance and a default value (1f) to avoid this behaviour.<br/>
<br/>
I didn&#39;t do much tests so it may break other things but for my purpose it is OK.<br/>
<br/>
[attachment on SourceForge]<br/>
http://sourceforge.net/tracker/download.php?group_id=78314&amp;atid=552834&amp;aid=1796298&amp;file_id=246030<br/>
PDFTextStripper.java.v0.7.3.patch (text/x-patch), 653 bytes<br/>
add a default space between words
  </td>
