                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows Vista, Eclipse, Java, Tomcat
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I use the PDF-Box mainly to manipulate forms which are generated with<br/>
the LifeCycle-Designer of Adobe. The main application of the PDF-Box is<br/>
to extract the XFA-part of a LCD-form and to write it back after manipulation.<br/>
 <br/>
All worked fine until I tried a LCD-form created with the newest LifeCycle-Designer<br/>
(version 8.2 I suppose). With such a form the PDF-Box doesn&#39;t find the XFA and<br/>
produces a Null-Pointer-Exception.<br/>
<br/>
Is there a solution for this problem?<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
