<br/>
I have attached an admittedly very complicated PDF document which (as far<br/>
as I can tell) features 90° and 135° rotated text in a 90° rotated page.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
Position-ordered text extraction gives horrible results. <br/>
<br/>
Normal text extraction is also very messy, although in this second case<br/>
the results are almost understandable. <br/>
<br/>
This is not the document I need to treat, but i think that if text can be<br/>
correctly extracted from that PDF, it should work for almost every other<br/>
existing PDF.<br/>
File Added: Flyer2.pdf<br/>
http://sourceforge.net/tracker/download.php?group_id=78314&amp;atid=552832&amp;file_id=279847&amp;aid=1981851
