</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When I tried to use the Maven files in JempBox, I got errors in the test code that it could not find the junit packages. Changing the pom file to better specify the test and source directories fixed it.  <br/>
<br/>
--- jempbox/trunk/pom.xml       (revision 723007)<br/>
+++ jempbox/trunk/pom.xml       (working copy)<br/>
@@ -36,7 +36,8 @@<br/>
        &lt;description&gt;JempBox is an open source Java library that implements Adobe&#39;s XMP(TM) specification.&lt;/description&gt;<br/>
<br/>
     &lt;build&gt;<br/>
-      &lt;sourceDirectory&gt;src&lt;/sourceDirectory&gt;<br/>
+      &lt;sourceDirectory&gt;src/org&lt;/sourceDirectory&gt;<br/>
+      &lt;testSourceDirectory&gt;src/test&lt;/testSourceDirectory&gt;<br/>
        &lt;/build&gt;<br/>
<br/>
   &lt;dependencies&gt;
  </td>
