                                            <td class="description">      Such as my attempt to extract plain text from PDF using PDFBOX:<br/>
<br/>
	PDFTextStripper stripper = new PDFTextStripper();<br/>
	stripper.setStartPage( 1);<br/>
	stripper.setEndPage( 5 );<br/>
	LucenePDFDocument document = new LucenePDFDocument();<br/>
	Document luceneDocument = document.convertDocument(file);<br/>
        System.out.println(&quot;CONTENTS: &quot;+luceneDocument.get(&quot;contents&quot;));<br/>
<br/>
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br/>
This is the result I get, and it never goes beyond page 1:<br/>
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br/>
<br/>
Document&lt;stored/uncompressed&lt;path:/home/alvin/Desktop/google.pdf&gt; stored/uncompressed&lt;url:/home/alvin/Desktop/google.pdf&gt; stored/uncompressed,indexed&lt;modified:20090130112759&gt; indexed&lt;uid:<br/>
Web Search Engine<br/>
Sergey Brin and Lawrence Page <br/>
Computer Science Department,<br/>
Stanford University, Stanford, CA 94305, USA<br/>
sergey@cs.stanford.edu and page@cs.stanford.edu <br/>
Abstract <br/>
In this paper, we present Google, a prototype of a large-scale search engine which makes heavy<br/>
use of the structure present in hypertext. Google is designed to crawl and index the Web efficiently<br/>
and produce much more satisfying search results than existing systems. The proto&gt;&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Is it Bug?
