                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Some PDF files store diacritics (accents over characters) as separate text elements. The PDF files essentially have a chunk of text and then backup and place the diacritic over one of the characters in the chunk of text. With text extraction, the current design does not allow the diacritic to be placed over a character in the chunk and instead it is placed after the chunk. <br/>
<br/>
The debug-diac2.pdf file in PDFBOX-429 shows this problem. 
  </td>
