</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        PDFBOX-90                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I had a requirement for adding page labels  (See PDF Reference<br/>
(http://www.adobe.com/devnet/acrobat/pdfs/PDF32000_2008.pdf, page 374<br/>
(12.4.2 Page Labels). Since PDFBox does not have this functionality<br/>
currently. I ended up implementing it. <br/>
<br/>
The code contains on public method getPageLabels(), which should become a part of the PDDocumentCatalog API. This method returns an array of page labels. The array size corresponds to the number of pages in the document.
  </td>
