</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The current pdfbox version extracts all needed data from a pdf document and uses lucene to create an index for the lucene search engine. <br/>
<br/>
To avoid the dependency on lucene pdfbox should only extract the data which can be used to create a lucene index outside from pdfbox. That would decrase the number of external jars and woukld eliminate an other potential issue because of changing apis like those coming with lucene 3.0. <br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ve created 2 new classes (one for the extraction and one as example how to use that feature) based on existing code and attached it as patch.<br/>
<br/>
WDYT?<br/>
<br/>
If that patch will be added to the trunk the existing code will be removed including both lucene jars.<br/>

  </td>
