</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      It&#39;s a good practice for a Java library to put all it&#39;s classes and other resources within a single package name hierarchy. To do this in PDFBox, I&#39;d like to move the resources we now have at /Resources to /org/apache/pdfbox/resources. This prevents potential naming clashes and makes things easier for downstream projects (like pdfbox-app) that want to repackage PDFBox.
  </td>
