                <tr id="issuerow12501158" rel="12501158" data-issuekey="PDFBOX-974" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    PDFBox
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="PDFBOX-974" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PDFBOX-974">PDFBOX-974</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                PrintPDF should not be case sensitive against printer name on Windows
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Wish</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Reopened
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Christophe Borivant
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Christophe Borivant
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 11/Mar/11 15:39 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 06/Nov/14 06:31 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.5.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Utilities            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP/ JRE 1.6.0_24
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Microsoft Os are mostly case insensitive.<br/>
If a printerName is given to PrintPDF, it looks for the provided string in a case sensitive manner ( line around 115 ).<br/>
<br/>
I made a little correction to the code to allow non case sensitive search on Windows os :<br/>
I changed :<br/>
{code}<br/>
                      if(printService[i].getName().indexOf(printerName) != -1)<br/>
                      {<br/>
                          printJob.setPrintService(printService[i]);<br/>
                          printerFound = true;<br/>
                      }<br/>
{code}<br/>
to :<br/>
{code}<br/>
                    if (isWindows())<br/>
                    {<br/>
                      if(printService[i].getName().toLowerCase().indexOf(printerName.toLowerCase()) != -1)<br/>
                      {<br/>
                          printJob.setPrintService(printService[i]);<br/>
                          printerFound = true;<br/>
                      }<br/>
                    }<br/>
                    else<br/>
                    {<br/>
                      if(printService[i].getName().indexOf(printerName) != -1)<br/>
                      {<br/>
                          printJob.setPrintService(printService[i]);<br/>
                          printerFound = true;<br/>
                      }<br/>
                    }<br/>
{code}<br/>
and added the method :<br/>
{code}<br/>
    public static boolean isWindows()<br/>
    {<br/>
        String os = System.getProperty(&quot;os.name&quot;).toLowerCase();<br/>
        return (os.indexOf( &quot;win&quot; ) &gt;= 0);<br/>
    }<br/>
{code}<br/>
I&#39;m not sure it&#39;s the best way to do it, but at least, it works !<br/>

  </td>
