                <tr id="issuerow12501440" rel="12501440" data-issuekey="PDFBOX-979" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    PDFBox
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="PDFBOX-979" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PDFBOX-979">PDFBOX-979</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                errors in %%EOF handling (fix included)
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Adam Nichols
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Timo Boehme
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Timo Boehme
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 15/Mar/11 09:23 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 02/Jul/11 16:28 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 16/Mar/11 16:40 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.6.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.6.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Parsing            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The &#39;%%EOF&#39; handling in PDFParser has several errors. The current implementation (start from line 467):<br/>
<br/>
                String eof = &quot;&quot;;<br/>
                if(!pdfSource.isEOF())<br/>
                    readLine(); // if there&#39;s more data to read, get the EOF flag<br/>
                <br/>
                // verify that EOF exists<br/>
                if(&quot;%%EOF&quot;.equals(eof)) {<br/>
                    // PDF does not conform to spec, we should warn someone<br/>
                    log.warn(&quot;expected=&#39;%%EOF&#39; actual=&#39;&quot; + eof + &quot;&#39;&quot;);<br/>
                    // if we&#39;re not at the end of a file, just put it back and move on<br/>
                    if(!pdfSource.isEOF())<br/>
                        pdfSource.unread(eof.getBytes(&quot;ISO-8859-1&quot;));<br/>
                }<br/>
<br/>
The problems:<br/>
- eof variable gets no value<br/>
- comparison if(&quot;%%EOF&quot;.equals(eof)) must be negated<br/>
- unreading must first add a newline or space byte because we read with readline() (like in bug PDFBOX-978)<br/>
<br/>
Corrected version:<br/>
                String eof = &quot;&quot;;<br/>
                if(!pdfSource.isEOF())<br/>
                    eof = readLine(); // if there&#39;s more data to read, get the EOF flag<br/>
                <br/>
                // verify that EOF exists<br/>
                if(!&quot;%%EOF&quot;.equals(eof)) {<br/>
                    // PDF does not conform to spec, we should warn someone<br/>
                    log.warn(&quot;expected=&#39;%%EOF&#39; actual=&#39;&quot; + eof + &quot;&#39;&quot;);<br/>
                    // if we&#39;re not at the end of a file, just put it back and move on<br/>
                    if(!pdfSource.isEOF()) {<br/>
                      	pdfSource.unread( SPACE_BYTE );	// we read a whole line; add space as newline replacement<br/>
                        pdfSource.unread(eof.getBytes(&quot;ISO-8859-1&quot;));<br/>
                    }<br/>
                }<br/>

  </td>
